      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Jugular vein suppurative thrombophlebitis or Lemierre's syndrome is a rare but distinct clinical entity. It should be considered in young, otherwise healthy adults with \"pharyngitis\" followed by high fever, painful swelling or pain in a latero-cervical area. Rapid and appropriate treatment is important to control this potentially fatal infection."},
